docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:3:This plan describes how to turn the current `/claim-support-review` surface into a stronger operator workflow for testimony capture, document intake, graph-backed evidence organization, vector retrieval, and legal sufficiency review.
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:16:- [templates/claim_support_review.html](../templates/claim_support_review.html) already provides an operator dashboard with coverage summaries, follow-up execution controls, manual review resolution, and recent follow-up history.
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:17:- [docs/APPLICATIONS.md](./APPLICATIONS.md) defines `/claim-support-review` as the operator review dashboard for claim support, parse-quality signals, follow-up execution, recent history, and manual-review resolution.
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:18:- [docs/PAYLOAD_CONTRACTS.md](./PAYLOAD_CONTRACTS.md) already exposes a substantial claim-support review contract, including `claim_coverage_summary`, `claim_support_gaps`, `claim_contradiction_candidates`, `claim_reasoning_review`, `follow_up_plan_summary`, and `follow_up_history_summary`.
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:30:The target workflow for `/claim-support-review` should be:
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:67:### 4. Make operator review explainable
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:77:| Claim support persistence | [mediator/claim_support_hooks.py](../mediator/claim_support_hooks.py) | strong review-state persistence exists | add durable fact registry and evidence-to-proof lineage |
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:80:| Vector retrieval | `integrations/ipfs_datasets/vector_store.py`, document optimization embeddings seam | available in adjacent workflow | add claim-review indexing and retrieval sessions |
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:83:| Operator dashboard | [templates/claim_support_review.html](../templates/claim_support_review.html) | coverage dashboard exists | expand into testimony/document/proof orchestration surface |
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:87:1. The dashboard is a review and follow-up surface, but not yet a guided testimony-capture surface.
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:93:7. Vector search is present elsewhere in the repo, but not yet a first-class retrieval plane for dashboard evidence review and question planning.
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:100:Extend `/claim-support-review` so the operator can enter or edit:
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:125:The ingestion workflow should emit a stable artifact record that can be linked into claim support, graph extraction, vector indexing, and proof analysis.
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:213:This addendum records a pre-implementation UI/UX review pass using Playwright screenshot artifacts from the unified workspace:
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:218:- `artifacts/ui-audit-layperson/screenshots/workspace-review.png`
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:221:The screenshot workflow did attempt to route those images through `MultimodalRouterBackend`. The multimodal review and text fallback both timed out, so the saved router artifact at `artifacts/ui-audit-layperson/reviews/iteration-01-review.json` is the deterministic fallback. That timeout is itself a P0 reliability finding: the review/optimizer path must return a bounded artifact and show the fallback reason in the workspace instead of leaving an operator guessing whether visual review actually occurred.
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:223:The visual review also expands the product target. The dashboard should not only help an operator review claim support. It should help a layperson create or respond to legal complaints while managing a docket of documents, inspecting and labeling those documents, annotating evidence spans, and asking grounded questions about the docket through `llm_router` and `multimodal_router`.
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:227:1. The current workspace is capability-rich but too dense for a stressed layperson. Intake, evidence, review, draft, Gmail import, MCP examples, release-gate metadata, and generated pleadings appear as long technical panels rather than a small set of obvious next actions.
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:228:2. The sticky bottom navigation can cover content in full-page screenshots, especially on intake, evidence, review, and draft. It should reserve layout space or collapse into a safer mobile/action-bar pattern.
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:231:5. Draft is visually overloaded. The release gate, checklist, composer, recommendations, and full pleading preview compete for attention. The layperson path should show one filing-readiness decision and one primary next action before exposing full document text.
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:235:9. Router and optimizer failures are too invisible. If `multimodal_router` times out or falls back to `llm_router`, the UI should say so plainly and preserve a review artifact.
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:236:10. Browser regression currently has two pre-implementation blockers: the unified workspace flow tried to click a hidden `#chat-open-profile` link, and the homepage flow expected a stale provider order string. Screenshot review should not depend on brittle hidden controls or outdated provider-order assertions.
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:253:Goal: make visual UX review reliable before implementation starts.
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:265:- ensure router calls are truly bounded and cannot leave progress stuck at `running_router_review`,
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:268:- add a screenshot-review test that succeeds with existing screenshots even when the full journey has unrelated failures.
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:272:1. Playwright can capture homepage, intake, evidence, review, draft, docket, document viewer, and chat screenshots in one reliable command.
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:273:2. Router review returns either a multimodal result or a deterministic fallback artifact within the configured timeout.
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:274:3. The workspace shows whether the latest UX review used `multimodal_router`, `llm_router`, or deterministic fallback.
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:308:- preserve annotation revisions and reviewer notes.
docs/CLAIM_SUPPORT_REVIEW_DASHBOARD_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md:380:1. Stabilize Playwright screenshot review and router fallback reporting.
