docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_BATCH1_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:51:If a change is primarily about graph-path scoring, theorem-prover orchestration, or review packet productization, it belongs to later batches.
docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_BATCH1_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:115:- preserve passage-level lineage needed for later support, contradiction, and predicate review
docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_BATCH1_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:129:- claim-support review summaries now consume provenance-backed normalized record summaries instead of relying only on parse-lineage fields
docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_BATCH1_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:149:- surface enough live-versus-archived lineage for later review and timeline drilldown
docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_BATCH1_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:153:- archived pages can participate in claim support and follow-up review as ordinary corpus artifacts
docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_BATCH1_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:184:- capture passage-level provenance needed for adverse-authority review, contradiction checks, and later predicate grounding
docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_BATCH1_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:189:- authorities with source text can participate in chunk-, fact-, and passage-level support review instead of remaining citation-only records
docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_BATCH1_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:199:- authority-derived facts now carry chunk and source-passage lineage so adverse-authority review, contradiction checks, and predicate grounding can trace facts back to parsed authority passages
docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_BATCH1_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:220:- keep review and follow-up payloads compatible while upgrading the source fact substrate underneath them
docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_BATCH1_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:234:- legal-authority facts now expose chunk IDs, chunk indexes, and source passage spans in the same normalized fact row shape used by downstream support review
docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_BATCH1_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:263:./.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_review_api.py -q
docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_BATCH1_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:266:Use the claim-support and review slice when parse, fact, or provenance changes alter the support substrate rather than only ingestion.
docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_BATCH1_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md:322:That slice had the highest leverage because provenance normalization was stable enough that the main remaining Batch 1 risk was archived-page corpus behavior drifting into an evidence-adjacent special case. Archived-page storage, support packets, and fact-backed review semantics are now covered more explicitly, so the remaining leverage is in keeping the broader cross-source fact contract enforced and documented without prematurely pulling in Batch 2 or graph-store redesign work.
