./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:221:- formal complaint claim payloads now preserve durable registry fields on `supporting_fact_entries` and embed claim-level `fact_registry_summary` under `support_summary` for drafting/proof-review consumers
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:243:- aggregate queue-state health counts across all matching jobs while keeping the returned job list bounded for operator previews
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:263:- persist claim-element-aware legal search programs with each stored authority so later review can explain why the authority was collected
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:279:- treatment data is available to support scoring and review payload generation
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:342:- evidence fact passage anchors now include bounded `source_passage.text` snippets alongside chunk IDs and offsets so review surfaces can show passage text without reopening the chunk table
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:362:- preserve authority-document lineage so review surfaces can trace support back to passage-level source text
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:369:- authority fact passage anchors now include bounded `source_passage.text` snippets alongside chunk IDs and offsets for passage-level review/proof traceability
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:370:- first-pass authority rule candidates now carry exact parsed passage anchors (`source_passage.text`, chunk id/index, offsets) plus shared parse lineage metadata so future predicate translation and review drilldowns can trace each candidate rule back to source text
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:432:- claim-support enrichment now carries graph lineage packets from stored evidence and authority `graph_metadata`, so review-oriented support links and derived fact rows can trace back to adapter snapshot semantics and source records
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:459:- review payloads now aggregate compact `graph_trace_summary` fields in `claim_coverage_summary` for dashboard and audit surfaces
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:461:- graph snapshot refs now carry compact adapter registry lookup payloads (`graph_snapshot_query` plus `graph_snapshot`) so review/coverage consumers can drill from persisted claim-support snapshot rows into queryable adapter snapshots and fact-registry coverage without issuing a second lookup
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:464:- mediator unresolved-gap queries now attach `graph_gap_context`, normalized `graph_gap_query`, and claim-level `graph_gap_query_summary` packets so review payloads and dashboards can distinguish graph-backed missing support from empty retrieval lanes without parsing raw GraphRAG results
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:468:- mediator can return graph-backed support traces for review and drafting readiness
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:487:- mediator wrappers expose coverage snapshot persistence and latest-snapshot retrieval for review and drafting consumers
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:488:- claim-support review payloads now expose coverage-matrix snapshot entries and lifecycle summaries alongside the live recomputed coverage matrix
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:491:- review payload `claim_coverage_matrix_snapshot_summary` now rolls those coverage snapshot path-health fields into a compact lifecycle summary, and the dashboard renders them as coverage snapshot chips
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:496:- drafting and review flows can ask for one authoritative claim-element coverage matrix instead of stitching multiple tables manually
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:526:- Compact ontology quality packets now include workflow/degraded-mode provenance plus gap type, severity, and follow-up-action count maps; review summaries and dashboard chips aggregate those fields for W5.1 operator triage.
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:551:- Claim coverage matrices and claim overviews now expose `support_quality_summary`, so review consumers can see support quality in addition to support counts.
./docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_EXECUTION_BACKLOG.md:573:- Denoiser review prompts now turn GraphRAG support-path quality signals into targeted questions about graph connectivity, source clarity, duplicate support, and direct support-path strengthening.
