docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:85:# Dedicated review surface mode
docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:86:python run.py --config config.review_surface.json
docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:91:For the focused operator workflow, `config.review_surface.json` starts only the claim-support dashboard and its review/follow-up API routes. The dashboard is available at `http://localhost:8000/claim-support-review`, and the dedicated review app exposes `http://localhost:8000/health` for lightweight health checks. The dashboard surfaces current coverage, lineage-aware follow-up signals, recent follow-up history, graph-backed source-context chips, and manual-review resolution controls from the same review payloads used by the API.
docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:201:If you only want the claim-support operator surface, create a dedicated service that uses `config.review_surface.json`:
docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:203:Create `/etc/systemd/system/complaint-generator-review.service`:
docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:217:ExecStart=/home/complaint-app/complaint-generator/venv/bin/python run.py --config config.review_surface.json
docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:231:Enable and start the review surface:
docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:235:sudo systemctl enable complaint-generator-review
docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:236:sudo systemctl start complaint-generator-review
docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:237:sudo systemctl status complaint-generator-review
docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:284:Each cycle writes status, logs, screenshots, optimizer reviews, and export-review artifacts under `artifacts/ui-optimizer-daemon/<user-id>`, so the morning handoff is a concrete trail of what changed and what the critic still wants fixed.
docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:362:For the review surface, the same reverse proxy pattern applies. The key operator routes are:
docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:364:- `/claim-support-review`
docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:365:- `/api/claim-support/review`
docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:371:curl -I http://127.0.0.1:8000/claim-support-review
docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:419:- Dedicated review surface: `/health`
docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:427:For the dedicated review surface service, probe `/health` instead:
docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:430:*/5 * * * * root curl -f http://localhost:8000/health || systemctl restart complaint-generator-review
docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:511:To build a review-surface-only image, swap the startup command:
docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:514:CMD ["python", "run.py", "--config", "config.review_surface.json"]
docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:560:For the dedicated review surface, mount `config.review_surface.json` instead and start with that config:
docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:564:      - ./config.review_surface.json:/app/config.review_surface.json:ro
docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:567:For a review-surface-only container healthcheck, target the dedicated health route:
docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:576:  -v "$PWD/config.review_surface.json:/app/config.review_surface.json:ro" \
docs/DEPLOYMENT.md:578:  python run.py --config config.review_surface.json
