docs/IPFS_DATASETS_PY_MILESTONE_CHECKLIST.md:316:The integration can be treated as mature when complaint-generator can acquire, archive, parse, organize, validate, and review legal support through one provenance-preserving workflow across full, partial, and degraded runtime modes.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:5:The review operator surface also has dedicated app factories for non-legacy deployments:
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:7:- `applications.create_review_api_app(mediator)` mounts only the claim-support review and follow-up execution API routes.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:8:- `applications.create_review_dashboard_app()` mounts only the `/claim-support-review` HTML dashboard.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:9:- `applications.create_review_surface_app(mediator)` mounts both the dashboard UI and the review/follow-up API routes on one FastAPI app.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:11:The repository also includes `config.review_surface.json` for launching the combined review surface through `run.py`, and `config.review_surface.huggingface_router.json` for launching that same surface against Hugging Face router/inference by default.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:15:The Complaint Generator provides two primary application interfaces and dedicated review-surface variants:
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:19:3. **Review Surface Apps** - Focused FastAPI apps for the claim-support dashboard and review APIs
